Falsifies `inter_process_communication::verification::receive_preserves_the_invariant`.

The defect: a receiver with nothing to collect joins the sender queue, the mirror of the slip
`send_preserves_the_invariant.patch` injects and in the mirror function. Kept as its own record
rather than folded into one, because each harness is evidence about its own operation and a
shared patch would leave either one unable to say it had been falsified.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(e.one_queue_invariant())`, on a rendezvous already
holding a queued receiver: both queues end up non-empty, and a later send would hand a receiver a
receiver as its rendezvous partner.

diff --git a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@ impl<T: Node> Rendezvous<T> {
         } else if let Some(sender) = self.senders.pop_front() {
             Receive::FromSender(sender, me)
         } else {
-            self.receivers.push_back(me);
+            self.senders.push_back(me);
             Receive::Blocked
         }
     }
